      "message": "fix(2d): cut an open Contour run on its air side\n\nA Contour on an open run of a part rode the run on the tool centre, so\nhalf the cutter cut the part the edge bounds (the gouge gate blocked the\npost). The new machining2d::contour_open_run reads the part sections at\nthe cut levels, finds the side without material and offsets the run by\nthe tool radius plus stock to leave to that side. Material on both\nsides, a side that changes, a tool that overlaps the part and a folding\noffset are refused by name. A run with no material beside it keeps the\ncentreline ride. Side applies to closed rings only.\n\nFixes #1777\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
